Subject: [CANDIDATE] drm/grate: release the per-buffer fence pointer arrays

Target: libre-tegra/linux bfffc6d6656e87f3de3aa4c09d852849081ef088 (7.0.1 reference).
Runtime leak reproduced on both 5.17 and 7.0.1: Xorg allocations from
 dma_resv_get_fences accumulate without matching frees. Pausing popsquares
 or switching to a running blank saver stops these allocations.
This source patch has not been compiled or installed.

The scheduler can consume all fence references and zero num_shared while
 the pointer array itself remains owned by the job. Free it regardless of
 that count during normal cleanup, and free successful earlier entries
 during error unwind. The modern dma_resv_get_fences clears and frees its
 own failed allocation, so the existing error-loop bounds remain unchanged.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/uapi/job_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/uapi/job_v2.c
@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@
 
 		for (k = 0; k < f->num_shared; k++)
 			dma_fence_put(f->shared[k]);
+
+		kfree(f->shared);
 	}
 }
 
@@ -573,6 +575,8 @@
 
 		for (k = 0; k < f->num_shared; k++)
 			dma_fence_put(f->shared[k]);
+
+		kfree(f->shared);
 	}
 
 	return err;
